    "summary": "The dev chat's named colours hold VS Code theme variables, and every fixed colour, tint and decorative gradient in the shell style, the row renderer style and the chat's markdown tokens is replaced by a name. One derived colour exists by the user's decision: the assistant message's ground. Both message bubbles take the chat request border; the whole chat uses the editor's monospace font; the colour scheme follows the theme kind; the history chip is a wrapper whose glyph is a mask in the text colour. The chat's own rules out-rank the shared sheet for the body and the diff container (the review finding on the revised design). High-contrast themes were not checked by eye; their behaviour is covered by the unit tests, as the revised design states.",
